PART 9 — A UNIFIED TIMELINE

14. Avoid confusing separate animation systems

The user should not have to guess whether a drawing belongs to Storyboard, Frame-by-frame or Animate.

I want a clear relationship between:

- Scene composition.
- Drawing frames.
- Character movement.
- Object movement.
- Effects.
- Typography.
- Camera.

Ideally, provide one scene timeline with separate visual tracks.

Example:

SCENE 01 — 10 seconds

BACKGROUND       ─────────────────────────

CHARACTER        ─────── pose / movement ───

BASKETBALL       ───── dribble ───────→ exit

EFFECTS                  impact / streaks

CAMERA           ───────────── zoom / shake

TEXT             ───── opening title ──────

A frame sequence can occupy a drawing track, while an object path occupies a motion track.

All tracks must use the same timebase.

If that cannot be implemented safely in the first release, design the data architecture for it and expose a clear, consistent interface rather than creating multiple incompatible timelines.


