THE FINAL PRODUCT STANDARD

The finished application should feel like a drawing app first, an animation studio second, and an AI production tool behind the scenes.

I should be able to open it and understand how to start drawing without reading a technical manual.

I should be able to sketch a rough stickman, design its background, add a butterfly, make the butterfly orbit around it, create a shape transformation, and organize everything without fighting the interface.

I should also be able to provide the exported project to a text-only OpenCode model and have it understand:

- What I drew.
- What each element represents.
- Where it is positioned.
- What the background contains.
- Which objects are in front or behind.
- How the character is posed.
- What moves.
- How it moves.
- When it moves.
- What should happen next.

Do not confuse a large number of controls with creative freedom.

Creative freedom comes from making complex ideas easy to express.

Build the application around that principle.